WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.912
This comparison is worth learning conceptually.

00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:07.322
GROUPING SETS produces only the grouping combinations you request.

00:00:07.322 --> 00:00:12.587
ROLLUP of A and B produces detail at A and B, a subtotal at A,

00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:16.237
and a grand total. It follows a hierarchy.

00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:22.352
CUBE of A and B produces detail, subtotals by A, subtotals by B, and the grand total.

00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:28.712
It generates every combination. A simple way to choose is to ask what report levels you need.

00:00:28.712 --> 00:00:32.482
If you need a hierarchy, ROLLUP is often a natural fit.

00:00:32.482 --> 00:00:37.522
If you need all cross-dimensional totals, consider CUBE.

00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:41.447
If you want only specific levels, GROUPING SETS gives you precise control.

00:00:41.447 --> 00:00:48.882
The SQL syntax is different, but the same grain reasoning still applies to every row produced.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:55.867
Connect this idea to a dashboard summarizing admissions by department and month.

00:00:55.867 --> 00:01:01.252
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:01:01.252 --> 00:01:08.882
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:01:08.882 --> 00:01:14.242
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:19.919
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
